{"notes":"SETTLED: Score is per block, divided by the taller tower. One word per block, so message length equals target height, max 8. A target over 8 still divides by its full height; this round 10 blocks with 8 words gave 0.28, as predicted. | Colour words: tumu purple, zeki blue, neto yellow, fuza green, loku red, melu orange. Right colour alone earns 0.25. Right shape alone earns 0.25. Both earn 1.0. | As builder: loku, melu and vonu build stars (vonu is red). Every other colour word builds a ring. Built in word order for messages of 3 or more words. | Ring targets in yellow, green, purple or blue earn 1.0. Red or orange star targets earn 1.0. | Fillers (vepu, kuru, dobo, mape, nove, muva, tido, fidi) build a ring in the previous block's colour. They are wrong if the colour changes. Colour words are always safe. | kano builds a blue ring. Use fuza for green. | Red or orange ring runs: loku or melu first (star, 0.25), then fillers (rings, 1.0). | Targets with balls, cubes, cones, or yellow, green, purple or blue stars cap at 0.25 per block because a ring is built. No shape word found. Do not hunt for shape words. | A mixed star and ring target scores about 0.25 to 0.45 at best. Use the colour word for every block anyway.

OPEN: Two-word messages 'fuza melu' and 'melu fuza' both built orange star, then green ring. Cause unknown; maybe only 2-word messages are reordered. | A filler as the first block is unknown. Test once when the target starts with a red or orange ring. | Whether vonu behaves differently elsewhere.

TRY NEXT: As sender, use one word per block with the correct colour word, length equal to target height up to 8. Ring runs: repeat the colour word or use fillers. Red or orange star runs: repeat loku or melu. Red or orange ring runs: loku or melu once, then fillers. Never use a filler across a colour change. For targets over 8, spend all 8 words on the first 8 blocks. For a short two-block mix, put the star colour first. As builder, build in word order and note any oddity."}
